# Database — safe changes only

- Migrations are ADDITIVE and backward compatible: the previous release must keep working after deploy and after a rollback.
  Add nullable columns or columns with defaults, new tables, new indexes.
- Never drop or rename a table or column, never delete or rewrite existing rows, unless the prompt explicitly says so and
  describes how existing data is kept. A destructive change is always a separate, owner-approved PR.
- Never edit a migration that is already on develop; write a new one. Filename date = today.
- Every migration has a working down().
- Enums are varchar columns backed by PHP enums. Money numeric(14,2). Translatable fields jsonb with ka required.
- Index foreign keys and filter columns. Soft deletes on listings.
- Update the model, its factory, and the seeder if the prompt touches demo data.
- Inspect the current schema with Boost `database-schema` first.
